## Why we moved the queue

The first block group opens the post. It is deliberately the shorter of the two, so a scorer that keeps only its top candidate drops it.

## What changed after the move

The second block group carries the bulk of the argument: latency fell, retries stopped piling up, and the on-call rotation got its weekends back.

It also has a second paragraph, which is exactly what used to make it the only block that survived extraction.

Ghost-style callout card: the last word on the migration.
